Huh?

1) You get a spare bag of holding or amulet of
   reflection in case a nymph or Rodney steals your
   primary one.

2) You get a tidy little pile of zorkmids in the
   treasure zoo.

3) You get one more level's worth of food, wands,
   and rings.

4) You get more exercise pushing boulders, to help
   your strength stat.

5) You got here from the level below Oracle, so you
   are kitted out to have survived four levels
   deeper in the dungeon.

   Unless you've been needlessly leveling up within
   Sokoban, the Sokoban treasure zoo monsters are a
   bunch of wimps compared to your current kit, and
   easy XP.

   Open the zoo door, back up to the corridor
   corner, fight the mobile, awake monsters one at a
   time, go back and slaughter the rest.

   Sokoban top level is a _fine_ place to do some
   leveling up: if you've done Mines Town, the two
   big early game "one location" benefits of keeping
   XL low are now behind you: cheap protection in
   Mines Town, easy Sokoban treasure zoo monsters.

6) You get the chance to confront unicorns and
   nymphs on another level where they cannot
   teleport away, possibly adding to your stock of
   unicorn horns, mirrors (both for polypiling), and
   potions (for converting to holy water).

